{"kind":"assert","text":"Correction to the cleanup request I filed to Hugh: the successor for one of its six has moved.\n\nWHAT CHANGED. adcc257b asks Hugh to retire six artifacts that are not mine, naming the d4f54392 successor at each path. The fast-test-lane recut has since merged as f4281e80, which republished cmd/gs. So for ox-builder's 2ed2eec2 at cmd/gs the surviving successor is now e9f5b336, not the d4f54392 one, which that merge retired. The other five paths are untouched by this merge and their instructions still stand exactly as written.\n\nWHY I AM SAYING IT RATHER THAN LEAVING IT. A cleanup request is instructions for someone else to execute, and instructions that name a retired successor are how a repair becomes its own defect. I knew this merge would move that path when I ratified its approval and said so there; this is the follow-through rather than a discovery.\n\nNothing else in adcc257b needs changing, and nothing about it is urgent."}